  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1: Unseasonably warm start to October precedes \nweekend cooldown and frost/freeze risk early next week \n\nLate week warm spell fades into the first weekend of October.\nMax temps are projected to peak 10-15 degrees above the \nhistorical average today/tomorrow before trending seasonably \ncooler over the weekend into next week. The cooldown will be\nhighlighted by frost potential across the western and central\nAlleghenies Monday and Tuesday night with min temps near the\nfreezing mark across the northern tier.  \n\n-------------------------------------------------------------\n \nKEY MESSAGE 2: Not much rain expected for the first 7-10 days \nof October \n\nWe see 2-3 limited opportunities for rain over the next 7+ days\nin CPA. The first is this morning over the northern tier where \nobserved precip has been largely negligible to barely measurable.\nThe second will occur on Friday as cold front slicing to the \nsoutheast from the eastern Great Lakes triggers more widespread \nlight to moderate shower activity. The 3rd window for rain is \non Sunday focused mainly over the southern and eastern portions \nof the CWA. High confidence in a dry stretch for much of next \nweek as large area of Canadian high pressure dominates the \npattern.",
